'''The Works''' was an industrial zone located in the [[Industrial District]] of [[Imperial City]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. It was a vast, burned out district that was mostly abandoned. The sector was largely flat and was covered in gases, smoke, and vapors pouring from those factories that were still standing.

==History==
The Works<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> was once a manufacturing powerhouse known throughout [[the galaxy]]. However, businesses which operated within the Works were eventually driven elsewhere due to the increasing cost of doing business on [[Coruscant]], leaving the once-booming industrial sector neglected and abandoned. Most [[Coruscanti]] started to avoid this area due to the high range of criminal activity that went on here.<ref name="CL2016" /><ref name="The Works">{{Databank|the-works|The Works}}</ref>

[[File:TheWorks-TSL.png|thumb|left|300px|The Works prior to the Clone Wars]]
Shortly after the [[Battle of Naboo]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Dooku]] traveled to the Works to confront [[Darth Sidious]] about his role in the death of [[Qui-Gon Jinn]]. Sidious assured Dooku that his actions were necessary for the greater good of the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]]. Unknown to Dooku, [[Yaddle]] had followed him and had heard the conversation. She pleaded with Dooku to return to the [[Jedi]], but Dooku [[Duel in the Works|fought]] and killed her on Sidious's orders.<ref name="The Sith Lord">{{TOTJ|The Sith Lord}}</ref>

At the start of the [[Clone Wars]], [[Count]] Dooku arrived in the [[Inquisitorius Headquarters|Coruscant tower]] located in the Works to inform Sidious, his [[Sith Master]], that the war between the Republic and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]] had begun. The [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lord]] was pleased at the news, as it brought them a step closer to the completion of the [[Sith]]'s [[Order 66|plan]].<ref name="AOTC" />

At the end of the Clone Wars, Sidious summoned Dooku back to the Works in response to [[Yoda]]'s presence on [[Moraband]]. Initiating a ritual using Dooku's [[blood]] to draw on his [[Force-bond]] with his old Master and feeding it with [[Force lightning]], Sidious was able to summon the [[Force power|power]] of [[dark illusion]] in an attempt to break Yoda's will.<ref name="Sacrifice">{{TCW|Sacrifice (episode)}}</ref>

In the ensuing [[Force vision|illusions]], the Jedi [[Grand Master]] saw himself with [[Anakin Skywalker]] and a [[squad]] of [[Clone trooper|clones]] on their way to the Works to apprehend the [[Sith Lord]]s, the intent being to break Yoda's spirit. During the illusion, Sidious [[Lightsaber combat|fought]] Yoda and attempted to force him to choose between saving Skywalker or killing Sidious. Yoda chose to save Skywalker, sacrificing himself. With this, the illusion ended and Sidious and Dooku's attempt to break Yoda failed.<ref name="Sacrifice" />

